        "21. Start with the customer, not the product\nA common mistake is to build a product first and search for customers later.",
        "Instead, understand a specific customer and the problem they want solved. The customer avatar is a practical reference document that helps keep marketing, product decisions, and sales communication focused.",
        "It should not be a fictional biography filled with invented details. It should be based on research, conversations, observed behaviour, and clearly labelled hypotheses.\nWhat to include in a customer avatar\nBasic context\n- Role, situation, or type of organisation.\n- Relevant experience level.\n- Buying authority and budget context.\n- Current tools or alternatives.\nProblem\n- What is not working?\n- How often does the problem occur?\n- What does it cost in time, money, effort, or opportunity?\n- What have they already tried?\n- Why have previous attempts failed?\nDesired outcome\n- What would a successful result look like?\n- How quickly do they want progress?\n- What would make the result valuable?\n- What risks do they want to avoid?\nBuying behaviour\n- How do they evaluate options?\n- Who influences the decision?\n- What objections do they raise?\n- What proof do they need?\n- What would make them act now?\nLanguage\n- How do they describe the problem?\n- What phrases do they use?\n- What questions do they ask?\n- What do they misunderstand?",
        "22. Research the customer with AI—and verify it\nAI can help organise research, but it cannot magically know the private thoughts of a market. Treat generated customer descriptions as hypotheses until you verify them.",
        "Useful inputs include:\n- Customer interviews.\n- Sales-call notes.\n- Support questions.\n- Reviews of competing products.\n- Public community discussions.\n- Search queries and frequently asked questions.\n- Your own experience delivering the service.\nCustomer research prompt\nAct as a customer-research analyst.",
        "I will provide information about a market, potential customers, and\nthe problem I may solve. Help me build a customer avatar grounded in\nthe evidence supplied.",
